{
  "quiz_html": "<h1> Pretest: Extrusion </h1>\n\n<form id=\"quizForm\">\n\n<p><b>Q1. Which country has maximum contribution in worldwide forging industry?</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"China\"> China</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"USA, Canada\"> USA, Canada</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"Europe\"> Europe</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"India\"> India</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q2. The types of extrusion process involved in metal forming are:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"3\"> 3</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"4\"> 4</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"1\"> 1</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"5\"> 5</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q3. Parameter which separates cold forming from hot forming is:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Re-crystallisation temperature\"> Re-crystallisation temperature</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Melting point\"> Melting point</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Physical\"> Physical properties</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Surface\"> Surface properties</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q4. How many types of presses are shown in extrusion module?</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q4\" value=\"3\"> 3</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q4\" value=\"10\"> 10</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q4\" value=\"1\"> 1</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q4\" value=\"5\"> 5</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q5. The force acting on the workpiece during extrusion is:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q5\" value=\"Compressive Force\"> Compressive Force</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q5\" value=\"Shear Force\"> Shear Force</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q5\" value=\"Tensile Force\"> Tensile Force</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q5\" value=\"Spring Back Force\"> Spring Back Force</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q6. Velocity of ram used in aluminium extrusion simulation:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q6\" value=\"1 mm/sec & 5 mm/sec\"> 1 mm/sec & 5 mm/sec</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q6\" value=\"2 mm/sec & 3 mm/sec\"> 2 mm/sec & 3 mm/sec</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q6\" value=\"5 mm/sec & 7 mm/sec\"> 5 mm/sec & 7 mm/sec</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q6\" value=\"4 mm/sec & 5 mm/sec\"> 4 mm/sec & 5 mm/sec</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q7. Die angles used in aluminium extrusion simulation:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q7\" value=\"45,60,90\"> 45°, 60°, 90°</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q7\" value=\"10,45,60\"> 10°, 45°, 60°</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q7\" value=\"20,40,60\"> 20°, 40°, 60°</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q7\" value=\"10,20,30\"> 10°, 20°, 30°</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q8. Metal extrusion is generally used to produce:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q8\" value=\"Both\"> Both</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q8\" value=\"Solid\"> Uniform solid section</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q8\" value=\"Hollow\"> Uniform hollow section</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q8\" value=\"None\"> None</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q9. For successive extrusion, the metal should be:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q9\" value=\"Ductile\"> Ductile</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q9\" value=\"Malleable\"> Malleable</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q9\" value=\"Plastic\"> Plastic</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q9\" value=\"Tough\"> Tough</label>\n<hr>\n\n<p><b>Q10. The extrusion chamber, die and ram are lubricated by:</b></p>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q10\" value=\"Solid lubricant\"> Solid lubricant</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q10\" value=\"Grease\"> Grease</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q10\" value=\"Vegetable\"> Vegetable</label><br>\n<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q10\" value=\"Kerosene oil\"> Kerosene oil</label>\n<hr><br>\n\n<button type=\"button\" onclick=\"checkQuiz()\" style=\"padding:10px 20px; font-size:16px;\">Submit Quiz</button>\n\n</form>\n\n<h2 id=\"result\"></h2>\n\n<script>\nfunction checkQuiz() {\n    const correctAnswers = {\n        q1: \"China\",\n        q2: \"3\",\n        q3: \"Re-crystallisation temperature\",\n        q4: \"3\",\n        q5: \"Compressive Force\",\n        q6: \"1 mm/sec & 5 mm/sec\",\n        q7: \"45,60,90\",\n        q8: \"Both\",\n        q9: \"Ductile\",\n        q10: \"Solid lubricant\"\n    };\n\n    let score = 0;\n    let total = Object.keys(correctAnswers).length;\n\n    for (let key in correctAnswers) {\n        let userAns = document.querySelector('input[name=\"' + key + '\"]:checked');\n        if (userAns && userAns.value === correctAnswers[key]) {\n            score++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    let accuracy = ((score / total) * 100).toFixed(2);\n\n    document.getElementById(\"result\").innerHTML =\n        '<b>Your Score: ' + score + '/' + total + '</b><br>Accuracy: <b>' + accuracy + '%</b>';\n}\n</script>"
}
